  "not_verified": [
    "Dates are sent as YYYY.MM.DD, the form of the documentation's payment example and of the Centas program; the documentation gives no date format for the other fields.",
    "The document and order fields are sent in the POST body, like the key; the documentation lists them as query parameters of a POST.",
    "Line values are sent as text with a point as decimal mark, as in the documentation's examples.",
    "Order lines carry the VAT rate as both pvm_tar and pvmtar, because the documentation names it both ways.",
    "Purchase invoice lines use the sales invoice's line fields; the documentation names none for purchases.",
    "Centas WS documents no duplicate check: sending the same invoice, order, payment or product again may create it again.",
    "How Centas matches the buyer of a sales invoice to an existing client (code, company code, VAT code or name) is not documented; the buyer group applies to a new buyer.",
    "Centas WS documents no required fields except for purchase invoices; the steps require the number, date, party name and lines.",
    "Which payments the payment export holds is not documented; Send bank payments stops without sending when a reference is already in it or it cannot be read.",
    "Totals are checked within one cent per line, because Centas lets each company choose how VAT is summed."
  ]
